In this case I'd be much more in favor of having two separate functions. A zero value has a different meaning from `nil`. 

```suggestion
// SetRunning sets the running state along with StartedAt time.
func (s *State) SetRunning(ctr libcontainerdtypes.Container, tsk libcontainerdtypes.Task, start time.Time) {
   setRunning(ctr, tsk, &start)
}

// SetRunningExternal is sets the running state without setting the `StartedAt` time (used for containers not started by Docker instead of SetRunning).
func (s *State) SetRunningExternal(ctr libcontainerdtypes.Container, tsk libcontainerdtypes.Task) {
   setRunning(ctr, tsk, nil)
}

